      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " This type provides a way to entirely opt-out of typical aliasing rules;",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            150,
            225
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " specifically, `&mut UnsafePinned<T>` is not guaranteed to be a unique pointer.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            226,
            308
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This also subsumes the effects of `UnsafeCell`, i.e., `&UnsafePinned<T>` may point to data",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            309,
            403
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " that is being mutated.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            404,
            430
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            431,
            434
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " However, even if you define your type like `pub struct Wrapper(UnsafePinned<...>)`, it is still",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            435,
            534
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " very risky to have an `&mut Wrapper` that aliases anything else. Many functions that work",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            535,
            628
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " generically on `&mut T` assume that the memory that stores `T` is uniquely owned (such as",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            629,
            722
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `mem::swap`). In other words, while having aliasing with `&mut Wrapper` is not immediate",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            723,
            815
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Undefined Behavior, it is still unsound to expose such a mutable reference to code you do not",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            816,
            913
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " control! Techniques such as pinning via [`Pin`] are needed to ensure soundness.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            914,
            997
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            998,
            1001
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Similar to [`UnsafeCell`](crate::cell::UnsafeCell), `UnsafePinned` will not usually show up in",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1002,
            1100
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " the public API of a library. It is an internal implementation detail of libraries that need to",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1101,
            1199
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " support aliasing mutable references.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1200,
            1240
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1241,
            1244
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This type blocks niches the same way `UnsafeCell` does.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1245,
            1304
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
